"{}",&#10; "\\negadelta": "\\nabla",&#10; "\\eqref": "\\href{###1}{(\\text{#1})}",&#10; "\\ref": "\\href{###1}{\\text{#1}}",&#10; "\\label": "\\htmlId{#1}{}",&#10; }&#10; });&#10; };&#10;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10; \[\]&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here is a good reference list of the pre-defined HTML colors: &lt;a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/named-color"&gt;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/named-color&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Crews (2018)</title><link>https://peppyhare.github.io/r/notes/scratch/crews2018/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://peppyhare.github.io/r/notes/scratch/crews2018/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="development-of-a-collisionless-plasma-kinetic-solver-and-an-investigation-of-one-dimensional-plasma-waves-and-instabilities"&gt;Development of a Collisionless Plasma Kinetic Solver and an Investigation of One-Dimensional Plasma Waves and Instabilities&lt;a class="anchor" href="#development-of-a-collisionless-plasma-kinetic-solver-and-an-investigation-of-one-dimensional-plasma-waves-and-instabilities"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Shielded potential of a test electron:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="https://peppyhare.github.io/r/katex/katex.min.css" /&gt;&#10;&lt;script defer src="https://peppyhare.github.io/r/katex/katex.min.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10;&lt;script defer src="https://peppyhare.github.io/r/katex/auto-render.min.js" onload="loadKatex();"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;script&gt;&#10; function loadKatex() {&#10; renderMathInElement(document.body, {&#10; delimiters: [&#10; { left: "$$", right: "$$", display: true },&#10; { left: "\\[", right: "\\]", display: true },&#10; { left: "$", right: "$", display: false },&#10; { left: "\\(", right: "\\)", display: false }],&#10; throwOnError: false,&#10; trust: (context) =&gt; ['\\htmlId', '\\href'].includes(context.command),&#10; macros: {&#10; "\\lcm": "\\mathop{\\mathrm{lcm}}",&#10; "\\sen": '\\text{sen}\\,',&#10; "\\dd": "\\mathop{\\mathrm{d} #1}",&#10; "\\abs": "\\lvert #1 \\rvert",&#10; "\\dd": "\\text{d}",&#10; "\\cross": "\\times",&#10; "\\pdv": "\\frac{\\partial #1}{\\partial #2}",&#10; "\\curl": "\\nabla \\cross #1",&#10; "\\vu": "\\mathbf{\\hat{#1}}",&#10; "\\vdot": "\\dot",&#10; "\\div": "\\nabla \\cdot #1",&#10; "\\grad": "\\nabla",&#10; "\\dv": "\\frac{d\\,#1}{d\\,#2}",&#10; "\\gr": "\\gamma",&#10; "\\vec": "\\mathbf{#1}",&#10; "\\tagl": "\\tag{#1}",&#10; "\\eqref": "(#1)",&#10; "\\laplacian": "\\mathbf{\\nabla ^2}",&#10; "\\label": "{}",&#10; "\\negadelta": "\\nabla",&#10; "\\eqref": "\\href{###1}{(\\text{#1})}",&#10; "\\ref": "\\href{###1}{\\text{#1}}",&#10; "\\label": "\\htmlId{#1}{}",&#10; }&#10; });&#10; };&#10;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10; \[\phi(r) = \frac{-e}{4 \pi \epsilon_0 r} e ^{- r / \lambda_D}\]&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;where the Debye length is &lt;span&gt;&#10; \( \lambda_D = \sqrt{\frac{\epsilon_0 T_e}{ n_e e}} \)&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;. The mean free path between large-angle collisions is estimated as&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Datta (2021)</title><link>https://peppyhare.github.io/r/notes/scratch/datta2021/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://peppyhare.github.io/r/notes/scratch/datta2021/</guid><description>&lt;span&gt;&#10; \[\]&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h1 id="a-domain-hybridized-plasma-model-using-discontinuous-galerkin-finite-elements"&gt;A Domain-Hybridized Plasma Model Using Discontinuous Galerkin Finite Elements&lt;a class="anchor" href="#a-domain-hybridized-plasma-model-using-discontinuous-galerkin-finite-elements"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="models"&gt;Models&lt;a class="anchor" href="#models"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Keep in mind that the behavior of a plasma is primarily determined by the ratio between a spatial length of interest and the following reference lengths. The appropriate model for describing a plasma depends on the regime defined by these lengths.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th&gt;Reference length&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Degree of magnetization&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Larmor radius \( r_L \)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Charge separation&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Debye length \( \lambda_D \)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Collisionality&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td&gt;Mean free path \( \lambda_{mfp} \)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="continuum-kinetic-model"&gt;Continuum Kinetic Model&lt;a class="anchor" href="#continuum-kinetic-model"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The continuum kinetic model is the most complete description, taking into account the forces acting upon each particle:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Drawing Diagrams</title><link>https://peppyhare.github.io/r/notes/scratch/drawing/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://peppyhare.github.io/r/notes/scratch/drawing/</guid><description>&lt;h3 id="graphics"&gt;Graphics&lt;a class="anchor" href="#graphics"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code class="language-goat" data-lang="goat"&gt; .&#10; 0 3 P * Eye / ^ /&#10; *-------* +y \ +) \ / Reflection&#10; 1 /| 2 /| ^ \ \ \ v&#10; *-------* | | v0 \ v3 --------*--------&#10; | |4 | |7 | *----\-----*&#10; | *-----|-* +-----&amp;gt; +x / v X \ .-.&amp;lt;-------- o&#10; |/ |/ / / o \ | / | Refraction / \&#10; *-------* v / \ +-&amp;#39; / \&#10; 5 6 +z v1 *------